  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "enter defensive state and interrupt the enemy's ultimate",
    "skill1": "deal multiple attacks while invincible",
    "skill2": "progressively grow stronger, each growth boosting ATK and enhancing attacks",
    "skill3": "battle penetration increase",
    "skill4": "ally buff triggers growth, expanding enhanced hit count",
    "skill5": "first ultimate interrupt drains extra energy from target"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Lily May]]'s opening defensive state can interrupt an eligible non-summoned enemy Ultimate and drain Energy, then she deals multi-hit damage during an **Invincible** window. Her growth increases ATK and adds max-HP damage, while temporary ally stat buffs accelerate that scaling. High-impact shells include **[[Lily May]]–[[Perseus]]–[[Ravion]]** with a tank and healer support, or **[[Alna]]–[[Lily May]]–[[Ravion]]** protection cores. Her interruption is most valuable when it catches the real eligible win condition; bosses and summons are exceptions. Pressure [[Lily May]] before growth completes, or use sustained coverage after her invincibility window instead of treating her as constantly repositioning.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Lily May]] threatens the first eligible Ultimate with an interrupt and gains a safe multi-hit window, so bait the cancel with a battle-start cast such as [[Niru]] before committing your real win button. When several Ultimates are ready, account for her frontmost or backmost targeting behavior; [[Eironn]] can also bait [[Lily May]] and enable the Wilder bonus. Do not burst into her invincibility; pressure her between windows or use lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]] while her growth is incomplete. [[Alsa]] adds root pressure after displacement in the [[Lily May]]–[[Scarlita]] matchup."
}
